Note: Calculator — EPL arithmetic showcase
Note: Run with: epl run examples/calculator/main.epl
Note:
Note: EPL has no expression-eval builtin, so rather than a REPL that reads
Note: arbitrary input, this demo computes every supported operation on a pair
Note: of sample values and prints a clean result table. It runs to completion,
Note: so the test suite can verify it stays correct on every release.

Say "╔══════════════════════════════════╗"
Say "║   EPL Calculator v1.0            ║"
Say "║   Arithmetic operations showcase ║"
Say "╚══════════════════════════════════╝"
Say ""

a = 12
b = 5
Say "Using a = " + to_string(a) + ", b = " + to_string(b)
Say ""

Say "  Addition        a + b = " + to_string(a + b)
Say "  Subtraction     a - b = " + to_string(a - b)
Say "  Multiplication  a * b = " + to_string(a * b)
Say "  Division        a / b = " + to_string(a / b)
Say "  Floor division  a // b = " + to_string(a // b)
Say "  Modulo          a % b = " + to_string(a % b)
Say "  Power           a ** b = " + to_string(a ** b)
Say ""

Say "  ── Math functions ──"
Say "    sqrt(b)     = " + to_string(sqrt(b))
Say "    abs(b - a)  = " + to_string(abs(b - a))
Say "    round(a / b) = " + to_string(round(a / b))
Say "    max(a, b)   = " + to_string(max(a, b))
Say "    min(a, b)   = " + to_string(min(a, b))
Say ""

Note: A small helper, to show functions and control flow too.
Function classify takes n
    If n % 2 == 0 Then
        Return "even"
    Otherwise
        Return "odd"
    End
End

Say "  ── Parity of 1..6 ──"
For Each n in [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
    Say "    " + to_string(n) + " is " + classify(n)
End
Say ""
Say "Done."
